course: dictionary
lesson: 2199
title: Counsellor: a helper who listens
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A counsellor is a person whose job is to listen to people and help them with their problems and feelings. Look at the clues in this sentence: «Some children carry very heavy memories, like war, for a long time; that is not weakness, and special help, such as a counsellor and a kind classmate, can make it lighter.» Heavy memories and lighter tell you that a counsellor helps people feel better.
explain: Counsellor can also mean someone who gives advice, which is a suggestion about what to do. «Counsellors can teach these skills» tells you that a counsellor can show you how to do something, such as counting to ten when you feel angry.
explain: The meaning can change from place to place. In the USA and Canada the spelling is «counselor», and a camp counselor is a young adult who looks after the children and runs the activities at a summer camp. Check the clues first: is the sentence about school, about a worry, or about a camp?
fact: A counsellor is a person trained to listen and help people with their problems and feelings.
fact: A school counsellor helps pupils who feel sad, worried or bullied.
fact: Talking to a counsellor is private, and it is a sensible, brave thing to do.
fact: In the USA and Canada the spelling is «counselor», and a camp counselor looks after children at summer camp.
fact: Useful phrases: school counsellor, talk to a counsellor, camp counselor, guidance counselor.
exercise: «Some children carry very heavy memories, like war, for a long time.» What is a counsellor? | A person who sells books in a shop | A person who drives the school bus | *A person trained to listen and help people with their problems and feelings | A person who only checks homework
exercise: «... special help, such as a counsellor and a kind classmate, can make it lighter.» What kind of help might a counsellor give? | A new bicycle | *Listening and support for feelings | A loud shout to stop the noise | A quick trip to the shops
exercise: At a summer camp in North America, what is a counselor? | A doctor who gives injections | A teacher who marks spelling tests | A person who cooks the dinner for the town | *A young adult who looks after the children and runs activities
test: Which sentence is true about talking to a counsellor? | *Talking to a counsellor is a sensible, brave thing to do | Counsellors never listen to anyone | Laughing at someone who sees a counsellor is clever | Only weak people talk to a counsellor
test: «Anyone can need help; laughing at someone for seeing a counsellor is unkind.» Why is laughing unkind? | Because it is a race, and laughing slows you down | Because counsellors only work at camp | Because counsellors are always cross | *Because anyone can need help, and the one laughing may need help one day too
exam: Jayden asks, «What is a school counsellor?» Which answer is best? | A teacher who only marks spelling tests | A shop that sells school bags | A bus driver for the school run | *A person trained to listen and help pupils who feel sad, worried or bullied
